      "answer": "$P(X=2)=\\frac37$.",
      "official_mark_scheme_text": "Method 1: $(6/10)(5/9)(4/8)(3/7)\\times4!/(2!2!)=3/7$. M1 valid product times integer permutation count; A1 (AG). Method 2: ${6\\choose2}{4\\choose2}/{10\\choose4}=15(6)/210=3/7$. M1 numerator combination product (consistent permutations condoned); A1. [2]",
      "structured": {
        "version": 1,
        "sections": [
          {
            "label": "Method 1",
            "steps": [
              {
                "working": "$\\dfrac6{10}\\dfrac59\\dfrac48\\dfrac37\\times\\dfrac{4!}{2!2!}$",
                "mark": "M1",
                "guidance": "Valid product multiplied by the integer permutation count."
              },
              {
                "working": "$\\dfrac6{10}\\dfrac59\\dfrac48\\dfrac37\\times6=\\dfrac37$",
                "mark": "A1",
                "guidance": "Answer given."
              }
            ]
          },
          {
            "label": "Method 2",
            "steps": [
              {
                "working": "$\\dfrac{\\binom62\\binom42}{\\binom{10}4}$",
                "mark": "M1",
                "guidance": "Numerator combination product; consistent permutations are condoned."
              },
              {
                "working": "$\\dfrac{15(6)}{210}=\\dfrac37$",
                "mark": "A1",
                "guidance": "Answer given."
              }
            ]
          }
        ],
